[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3664826382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114089#issuecomment-3664826382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114089","id":3664826382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7acNAO","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-17T11:00:59Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T11:00:59Z","body":"I don't know the XR system here but not sure this is on the Godot side, unless the engine somehow blocks these inputs specifically based on how we do things, if the engine enters an invalid state or breaks it can't really do anything \"right\", so not sure how this can be avoided other than making sure the engine exits cleanly if it encounters some error. Unless other programs running on this platform behave differently when locking up or crashing I'd suspect this is a platform issue of not making system menus available in this case\n\nBut if it's purely a soft locked issue with the engine somehow still running but not making input available that could be an engine problem, but that might also be a user error in the code of your project, AFAIK the engine will just shut down if it fails to load the game at the start, unless you mean a loading screen inside the game itself, then I'd suspect it's based on the code of the game project not the engine","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3664826382/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3667140015","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114089#issuecomment-3667140015","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114089","id":3667140015,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7alB2v","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-17T21:00:28Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T21:01:55Z","body":"> the engine enters an invalid state or breaks\n\nIt's not an error in the engine, it's my GDScript. In order to see my error I need to pause the app via hand tracking.\n\nHere's how my workflow normally looks. I run the game, an error occurs, so I open the editor back up. All is well. I used hand tracking to exit.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c74f19df-8f39-49df-879f-ef9fd0b705a2\n\nBut what if I hit a breakpoint/error in _ready() before the game is fully loaded? Now I'm stuck in the loading screen. I can't use hand tracking for some reason. I have to resort to controllers, which I find tedious.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68adb58e-985f-45a6-883a-7b8e0e5e2876","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3667140015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3667150268","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114089#issuecomment-3667150268","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114089","id":3667150268,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7alEW8","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_ur